    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The audit output confirms the end state:\n\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\n \"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe memberId carries the V2 region (`NSWV2`), yet `ownerSegment` is still `STANDARD_METRO` (derived from the *plain* region), confirming the tag stayed out of the segment.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity, keeping each change in the unit responsible for it:\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in)**\n- New `util/OwnerIdentityVersion` owns the version number (`2`), the fixed `\"V2\"` tag, and the two mixing rules: `regionCode(plainRegion)` (appends the tag \u2192 `NSWV2`) and `stampHashInput(input)` (prefixes `V2|` before hashing). This is the single source of the version policy, reused everywhere.\n- `MemberIdGenerator` now embeds the V2 region code in the `<REGION>` segment.\n- `HouseholdIdGenerator` and `Owner.getIdentityKey()` now hash the V2-stamped input.\n- Because the tag can never appear at those positions under v1, no v1 value is reproduced.\n\n**Response shape**\n- `openapi.yml`: removed top-level `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`, added a nested `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping them, added an integer `apiVersion`, and clarified that `locality` is the plain region.\n- `OwnerMapper` maps `apiVersion` and builds the `identity` object; `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` remain plain-region derived.\n\n**Audit schema + owner segment**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion` (2) and `ownerSegment`.\n- `OwnerAuditor` recomputes the owner segment via the mapper and includes it; the event's `memberId` is now the V2 value automatically.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) were left untouched. `mvn -o test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS.",
