    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is implemented by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:120`), takes an `OwnerFieldsDto` body, and calls into `ClinicServiceImpl`.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, failures \u2192 400 via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull @NotBlank @Size(1..30) @Pattern(letters, up to 3 words)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull @NotBlank @Size(1..30) @Pattern(letters, up to 3 words, optional trailing dot)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull @NotBlank @Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull @NotBlank @Size(1..20)` + custom `@Telephone` (must normalize to E.164 with valid national length)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Email @Size(1..255)` + custom `@NotDisposableEmail` (rejects disposable domains)\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Pattern(MR|MRS|MS|DR)` (optional)\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 each `@Size(1..255)`\n   - **class-level** `@ValidPostcode` \u2014 postcode must be 4 digits and within the city's region range if the region is known (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099); null passes\n   - **class-level** `@ValidAddress` \u2014 requires a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** `address`\n\n3. **Registration date not in the future** \u2014 `isRegistrationDateInFuture`; else 400 `BusinessRuleViolationException`.\n\n4. **Daily owner limit** \u2014 `isDailyOwnerLimitReached` (\u2265 100 for that date); else 429. *(Checked after the date is resolved to a business day \u2014 see side-effect 2.)*\n\n5. **City at capacity** \u2014 `isCityAtCapacity` (\u2265 50 owners in that city); else 409.\n\n6. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 `existsOwnerWithIdentityKey`, comparing the SHA-256 identity hash against non-deleted owners sharing the telephone; else 409.\n\n7. **Entity-level validation at persist** \u2014 Hibernate re-validates the `Owner`/`Person` entity on save: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, and `telephone` `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`.\n\n## Side-effects / mutations (in order)\n\n1. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if seen before, short-circuits and returns the original owner with **200 OK** (no new work).\n\n2. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping with normalization** (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`): telephone normalized to E.164, address normalized and composed (structured `addressLine1/2` preferred over flat `address`), and `Owner.setEmail` lower-cases the email.\n\n3. **Registration date resolved** \u2014 `resolveRegistrationDate`: null defaults to today, then rolled forward off weekends to a business day; set back on the owner.\n\n4. **Household assignment** \u2014 `assignHousehold`: if postcode present, sets a deterministic `householdId` from `lastName` + postcode.\n\n5. **Derived fields set on the owner:**\n   - `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of same first+last name (case-insensitive)\n   - `householdSize` \u2014 existing household members + 1\n   - `membershipLevel` \u2014 derived level, capped to max household member level + 1\n   - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 > 80 registrations that day\n   - `capacityWarning` \u2014 city count in [40, 50)\n\n6. **Possible-duplicate detection** \u2014 only when `sharesHousehold` is not true: same postcode + last-name Soundex but different identity key sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n7. **Save** (`saveOwner`): for a new owner, generates a `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` with Luhn check digit) and de-duplicates it against the repo, then `ownerRepository.save(...)`. On persist, the entity's `@PrePersist` re-defaults/rolls the registration date again.\n\n8. **Audit** \u2014 `ownerAuditor.auditCreated`: writes a human-readable line plus a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (type `OWNER_CREATED`, monotonic sequence) to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n9. **Welcome notification** \u2014 `welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome`: writes a line to the `NOTIFY` logger (no real email sent).\n\n10. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 `idempotencyStore.record(key, owner.getId())` in an in-memory map (first-write-wins; blank keys ignored).\n\n11. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the registration date gets resolved/rolled **twice** (once in the service, again in the entity's `@PrePersist`), and `sharesHousehold` is accepted on input but documented as write-only/never persisted (it only gates the possible-duplicate check)."
